n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":27708817},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1DQMCBX32KDVWBJBF8W1\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ4SNEC), short refs like @01KJ4SNE fail. kspec already has a shortest-unique-ID utility — this should be used anywhere refs are displayed (triage list, task list, inbox list, promote result_ref, etc.) so that presented refs are always unambiguous and copy-pasteable into subsequent commands.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:01.300Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQA0MV956KKZREMG980AE6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:37:42.812Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g., 01KJ4SNE9... and 01KJ4SNEC...), the default 8-character short ref `@01KJ4SNE` is ambiguous and fails to resolve. The `ReferenceIndex.shortUlid()` method (in `src/parser/refs.ts` line 310) already computes the minimum unique prefix, but many places in the codebase use a hardcoded `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` instead. There are 69 occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` across 19 files.\\n\\n**Where**: All places that format ULID refs for display need to use `shortUlid()` instead of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)`. Key files with hardcoded slicing:\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` (14 occurrences) — triage list, record, act, get, start\\n- `src/cli/commands/inbox.ts` (9 occurrences) — inbox list, add, promote\\n- `src/cli/commands/item.ts` (6 occurrences) — item list, get, add\\n- `src/cli/commands/plan.ts` (9 occurrences) — plan list, get\\n- `src/cli/commands/search.ts` (4 occurrences) — search results\\n- `src/cli/commands/session/context.ts` (4 occurrences) — session context display\\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` (1 occurrence) — promote result ref\\n- `src/parser/validate.ts` (8 occurrences) — validation output\\n- Several other files with 1-3 occurrences each\\n\\nThe `ReferenceIndex` is already available in most of these contexts (it's built during `initContext()` or `buildIndexes()`).\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. For each file, replace `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` with `index.shortUlid(_ulid)` where a ReferenceIndex is in scope\\n2. For files where no index is available, either thread the index through or create a lightweight shortening utility\\n3. For triage records (which aren't indexed in the main ReferenceIndex), consider building a local index or a dedicated triage ULID shortener\\n4. Ensure that refs displayed by any list/get/result command are always copy-pasteable into subsequent commands without ambiguity\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- No occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` remain in display-facing code paths\\n- All displayed refs (triage list, task list, inbox list, search results, promote result_ref, etc.) use `shortUlid()` or equivalent\\n- A test with two items sharing an 8-character ULID prefix shows that displayed refs are still unique and resolvable\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\",\n      \"title\": \"Semantic Exit Codes\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"when\": \"operation succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"user input is invalid\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"command is cancelled by user\",\n          \"when\": \"confirmation prompt declined\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters runtime error\",\n          \"when\": \"operation fails during execution\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"command finds nothing\",\n          \"when\": \"query returns no results\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0 with empty result set\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command used incorrectly\",\n          \"when\": \"invalid flags or arguments provided\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1 with usage information\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"batch operation completes\",\n          \"when\": \"partial failures occur\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command documentation\",\n          \"when\": \"developers implement commands\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code meanings documented in code\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-dry-run\",\n      \"title\": \"Dry Run Preview Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports dry run\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"show what would be changed without applying\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes\",\n          \"then\": \"no files are modified\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"output is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"clear indication that this is a preview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command would error\",\n          \"then\": \"error shown but no state changed\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"--dry-run and --force both provided\",\n          \"when\": \"command executes\",\n          \"then\": \"dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run --json provided\",\n          \"then\": \"JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","status":"completed"}